cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "No Magic Smoke: A Brain-Friendly Guide to the AMD UltraFast Design Methodology"
message: "If you use or adapt this guide, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Badjian
    given-names: Mehdi
repository-code: "https://github.com/mehdibadjian/no-magic-smoke-fpga"
url: "https://mehdibadjian.github.io/no-magic-smoke-fpga/"
abstract: >-
  An independent, unofficial study companion to the AMD UltraFast Design Methodology,
  covering board and device planning, timing constraints and clock domain crossing, RTL
  and IP design, implementation and timing closure, power and thermal management, and
  hardware debug. Written in the Head First pedagogical style, with every analogy mapped
  onto named silicon and tool commands, a worked calculation in every section, and
  answers to every question posed. Conformance to the authoring contract is enforced
  programmatically in CI.
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - AMD
  - Xilinx
  - UltraScale
  - Vivado
  - UltraFast Design Methodology
  - timing closure
  - clock domain crossing
  - technical education
license: CC-BY-4.0
